// Trading: the player asked "Want to trade?". "~ open_trade" opens the trade screen once the pony's
// lines have been read. A pony can turn you down in their own words - that's a consequence, not a
// punishment: it tells you something about them.
//
// PLACEHOLDER LINES - a scaffold showing the shape; every line here is meant to be rewritten.


=== nothing_to_trade
start: trade
weight: 100
when: profession(none)
{pony}: Trade? Oh, I don't really have anything to sell.

=== not_today
start: trade
weight: 50
when: not profession(none), mood(grief, strong)
{pony}: ...Not today. I'm sorry.

=== sure
start: trade
when: not profession(none), not mood(grief, strong)
{pony}: Sure! Take a look.
    or: Of course - see anything you like?
~ open_trade

=== cranky
start: trade
weight: 3
when: not profession(none), not mood(grief, strong), personality(cranky)
{pony}: Fine. Make it quick.
~ open_trade

=== friend
start: trade
weight: 3
when: not profession(none), not mood(grief, strong), fondness >= high
{pony}: For you? I'll even throw in a smile. Have a look!
~ open_trade
